Note: EPL Email Package — Basic Usage Examples
Import "epl-email"

Say "=== EPL Email Demo ==="

Note: Create SMTP mailer (Gmail example)
Say "Creating mailer..."
Set mailer to create_mailer("smtp.gmail.com", 587, "your-email@gmail.com", "your-app-password")
Say "Mailer configured for smtp.gmail.com:587"

Note: Send a simple email
Say ""
Say "--- Sending plain text email ---"
send_email(mailer, "recipient@example.com", "Hello from EPL!", "This email was sent using the EPL programming language.")
Say "Email sent!"

Note: Send HTML email
Say ""
Say "--- Sending HTML email ---"
Set html to "<h1>Welcome to EPL</h1><p>Write code the way you think.</p>"
send_html_email(mailer, "recipient@example.com", "Welcome!", html)
Say "HTML email sent!"

Note: Templates
Say ""
Say "--- Using templates ---"
Set welcome_tpl to create_template("Hello {{name}}! Your account {{email}} is ready. Your plan: {{plan}}")
Say "Template created"

Set rendered to render_template(welcome_tpl, dict())
Say "Rendered: " + rendered

Note: Email validation
Say ""
Say "--- Validation ---"
Set valid1 to validate_email_address("user@example.com")
Say "user@example.com valid: " + valid1

Set valid2 to validate_email_address("not-an-email")
Say "not-an-email valid: " + valid2

Set domain to extract_domain("ceo@company.io")
Say "Domain of ceo@company.io: " + domain

Say ""
Say "=== Done! ==="
